From ccabe82758416f4c0402133191a37d4eee22c6a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:58:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep failed Kanban reads invocation-local and fail
 closed on done

Replace the shared per-sid failure marker with an explicit card_read_failed
return flag from _card_items through _live_work. Before derived completion,
retain stored waiting/decision outcomes on a failed read, otherwise emit
unresolved/card_read_failed. Valid declarations and provider decisions retain
precedence, and successful silent cron completion cannot bypass the guard.

P2 choice: remove the card-id/cue-word heuristic, rather than trying to infer
negation and historical tense from keyword co-occurrence. The explicit read
failure guard covers the observed board-busy bug without demoting completed
replies containing 'No remaining work' or historical 'not yet running'.
Successful-but-incomplete projection is a separate ownership/projection seam,
not evidence this prose heuristic can safely establish.

Five whys (owner card t_01a1cd4e2e9d1304 comment 189496):
1. The chat was green because its stored outcome was done/derived; Desktop
   logged waiting->done while still listing the open card t_c850e0f6.
2. _derive_current saw no waits because _guarded("kanban cards") returned
   empty lists after logging the unavailable card source at 00:54:50Z.
3. BoardLifecycleBusy reported database is locked while update admission
   was paused (backend_retirement).
4. The judge failed with UnscopedSecretError, then looks_like_summary accepted
   the closing-looking reply as done.
5. _guarded's empty fallback conflated failed reads with confirmed no work.
Root happened: derived done lacked affirmative live-work evidence.
Root not caught: tests covered successful reads, not session_tasks failures;
PR1136 remained changes-requested without an owner. Earlier false-green
occurrences included t_088df457 and t_01a1cba407f15223.
Countermeasures: explicit per-invocation status, parent-RED regressions, and
hub owner t_01a1cd4e2e9d1304 for exact-head review, ship, and live lock replay.

Proof: the eight BoardLifecycleBusy cases fail on 78c57a02's parent
7026994c9b80916b094add04c640da3131173e3c. Rebased old implementation fails
12 new cases including deterministic same-sid interleaving and P2 controls.
After repair, test_session_outcome.py: 102 passed, 0 failed; health: zero
blocking/advisory findings. No merge or deployment performed in this task.
